gosh seam 02: Each end measures how much of what it is sent does not arrive, and tells the other.

For:   REQ1/FWD-2. A UDP datagram too large for one frame is sent in fragments, and whether to add
       parity to them follows the loss the path really has. mosh already numbers every datagram,
       so the receiver can count the ones missing; only the sender can use the answer.
What:  Connection counts, from the sequence numbers it already reads in recv_one, the share of
       the peer's datagrams that did not arrive (measure_loss; get_recv_loss). The sender reports
       it in a second optional field, recv_loss (field 1002), only alongside capabilities, so a
       stock mosh is never sent it. The receiver keeps what the peer reported (sidechannel_loss).
Where: Connection (two constructors, recv_one, and a new function beside port());
       transportinstruction.proto; TransportSender::send_in_fragments; Fragmenter::make_fragments;
       Transport (its constructors and recv).
Kind:  additions only. It must be inside recv_one: the sequence number is a local there.
Needs: 01-capabilities.
Pin:   upstream mosh at decd9b705eb81626f694335b8d5940538beb06da; cut against the result of the patch before it.
From:  the fork, wmacevoy/mosh at mosh-1.4.0-pf.7; the text added is the fork's, unchanged.

